<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello, i noticed strange behaviour of my brand new MD9600 with latest firmware release: fan start to turn for a couple of seconds when manually switching from some channel to another  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_lol.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":lol:" title="Laughing"> <br>It seems to be funny, but this slows radio commands annoyingly.<br>In VFO mode nothing happens.<br>I'm the only one?</div></blockquote>The firmware doesn't have any control on the fan.<br><br>I bet the famous channels have APRS beaconing defined, hence the transceiver is transmitting (then the fan starts).</div></blockquote>Yessss!. No TX led, no meters on my power supply, who could know that radio switch in TX every channel change?  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_lol.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":lol:" title="Laughing"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=558">IK1HJT</a> — Sat Apr 12, 2025 12:01 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
